.git/
.github/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
venv/

# large / generated — these live in named volumes, never in the image
data/
# ...except the tokenizer, which the root Dockerfile COPYs at build time. A COPY whose
# source is entirely dockerignored is a hard build failure ("file does not exist"), not a
# silent skip, so `data/` alone made that image unbuildable. Keep this negation and the
# Dockerfile's COPY in sync.
!data/nano/tokenizer/
runs/
ckpt/
export/
reports/
*.pt
*.bin
*.safetensors
wandb/

# docs & blueprint noise not needed at build time
*.md
!README.md
.claude/
specs/
